{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdajAotKtrRJDL8FqXmT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the convergence failure, and the repaired candidate `bayesian_generator_personal_suspicion` now passes the admission self-check (`OK`). It still has to pass novelty, which the self-check doesn't test, and admission's full 4×4000-draw fit, which I couldn't run here.\n\n**Hypothesis (unchanged):** people work out how probable it is that each sequence came from a fair coin rather than from a non-random generator: a biased coin, a sticky or switchy coin, or a mirror- or complement-symmetric construction. The one distortion is a personal prior suspicion that a sequence was made non-randomly. That changes which pairs each person can tell apart, which bears on the critique's finding that people differ in how often they agree with the majority choice.\n\n**Why the first attempt failed to converge:** the fitted suspicion sits where the posterior is close to exponential in the evidence. There, raising the suspicion and raising decisiveness have the same effect, so the two traded off along a ridge (the fit ran away to suspicion ≈ 5 and decisiveness ≈ 95). People who guess a lot could also sit at either extreme of suspicion, which split their estimates into two modes.\n\n**What I changed:**\n- **Decisiveness rescaled:** it is now measured per unit of log evidence at a typical sequence, i.e. divided by each person's posterior slope there. This removed the ridge while keeping the curvature, which is what the hypothesis is about.\n- **Tighter priors on suspicion:** population mean Normal(0, 1), between-person spread HalfNormal(0.5), non-centred. With a wider spread prior the spread drifted, because past a point extra suspicion stops changing the predictions.\n- **Shared guessing rate:** the personal guessing rate was replaced by one shared rate with a Beta(2, 18) prior, which removes another parameter that traded off with the others.\n\n**Test fit (2 chains, 500 tune + 500 draws, target_accept 0.99):** no divergences, R-hat 1.00 on every parameter, minimum bulk ESS 580 (the gate needs ≥ 100). Two caveats:\n- The between-person spread of suspicion is only weakly identified (0.41, 94% interval 0 to 0.94), so the \"personal\" part of the hypothesis gets little support from this data.\n- On the self-check's one-chain smoke fit, PSIS-LOO came out unreliable: 4.9% of trials have Pareto k > 0.5, against a 1% tolerance. If that holds in the full fit, the model may not be eligible for export.\n\nAll three files are written in `candidate_1_repair_1/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":940,"cache_read_input_tokens":95173,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":940,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5465e775-b45e-4811-80f2-f82dc9b491cc","uuid":"089db7a9-61e5-401a-9921-a5cd1a4cf469","timestamp":"2026-10-02T14:39:29.421Z","request_id":"req_011Cfdaj9s4yZqGzxRiwNTHm"}
